body:
I've had Opus also have a go at this, and it came back with an even faster version it seems (based on the output by the benchmark script by @kjk, shared above):

| Input | Original | EarlyFast | MergedFixed | CachedLen | Tiered |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Single CJK "字" | 7.9ms | 5.7ms | 3.7ms | **3.6ms** | 3.8ms |
| Single Latin "A" | 7.8ms | 5.8ms | **4.4ms** | 4.6ms | **4.4ms** |
| CJK string | 8.0ms | 5.5ms | 4.5ms | **4.3ms** | **4.3ms** |
| Latin string (34ch) | 117ms | 41.3ms | 34.7ms | **28.7ms** | 34.8ms |
| Mixed string | 28.6ms | 11.6ms | 9.6ms | **9.5ms** | **9.5ms** |

Speedup over original:

| Input | EarlyFast | MergedFixed | CachedLen | Tiered |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Single CJK | 1.4x | 2.1x | **2.2x** | 2.1x |
| Single Latin | 1.3x | **1.8x** | 1.7x | **1.8x** |
| CJK string | 1.5x | 1.8x | **1.9x** | **1.9x** |
| Latin string | 2.8x | 3.4x | **4.1x** | 3.4x |
| Mixed string | 2.5x | **3.0x** | **3.0x** | **3.0x** |

Here're the functions:

```ts
// --- Winner A: MergedFixed — best for CJK-heavy workloads ---
// charCodeAt loop + merged adjacent ranges + frequency-ordered BMP checks +
// correct surrogate handling (after BMP checks, not inside c < 0x3000).
// Fewest comparisons for CJK Unified (0x4E00-0x9FFF): c < 0x3000 → false,
// c >= 0x4E00 && c <= 0x9FFF → true (2 comparisons total).
export function isCJKMergedFixed(s) {
  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    const c = s.charCodeAt(i);

    if (c < 0x3000) continue;
    if (c >= 0x4e00 && c <= 0x9fff) return true;   // CJK Unified (most common)
    if (c <= 0x30ff) return true;                    // Symbols + Hiragana + Katakana
    if (c >= 0x3400 && c <= 0x4dbf) return true;    // Extension A
    if (c >= 0xac00 && c <= 0xd7af) return true;    // Hangul
    if (c >= 0xff00 && c <= 0xffef) return true;    // Fullwidth Forms
    if (c >= 0xf900 && c <= 0xfaff) return true;    // Compat Ideographs

    // Supplementary planes — decode surrogate pair
    if (c >= 0xd800 && c <= 0xdbff && i + 1 < s.length) {
      const lo = s.charCodeAt(i + 1);

      if (lo >= 0xdc00 && lo <= 0xdfff) {
        const cp = ((c - 0xd800) << 10) + (lo - 0xdc00) + 0x10000;
        i++;

        if (
          (cp >= 0x20000 && cp <= 0x2a6df) ||    // Extension B
          (cp >= 0x2a700 && cp <= 0x2b81f) ||    // Extensions C+D (merged)
          (cp >= 0x2b820 && cp <= 0x2ebef) ||    // Extensions E+F (merged)
          (cp >= 0x2f800 && cp <= 0x2fa1f) ||    // Compat Supplement
          (cp >= 0x30000 && cp <= 0x3134f)       // Extension G
        ) {
          return true;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return false;
}

// --- Winner B: CachedLen — best for Latin-heavy workloads ---
// Same as MergedFixed but caches s.length in a local variable.
// Saves a property access per loop iteration (+18% for 34-char Latin strings).
// Tradeoff: the upfront `const len = s.length` costs ~0.4ns, which causes
// -10% regression when the loop exits in 1 iteration (CJK strings).
// Break-even at ~2 iterations.
export function isCJKCachedLen(s) {
  const len = s.length;

  for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) {
    const c = s.charCodeAt(i);

    if (c < 0x3000) continue;
    if (c >= 0x4e00 && c <= 0x9fff) return true;
    if (c <= 0x30ff) return true;
    if (c >= 0x3400 && c <= 0x4dbf) return true;
    if (c >= 0xac00 && c <= 0xd7af) return true;
    if (c >= 0xff00 && c <= 0xffef) return true;
    if (c >= 0xf900 && c <= 0xfaff) return true;
    if (c >= 0xd800 && c <= 0xdbff && i + 1 < len) {
      const lo = s.charCodeAt(i + 1);
      if (lo >= 0xdc00 && lo <= 0xdfff) {
        const cp = ((c - 0xd800) << 10) + (lo - 0xdc00) + 0x10000;
        i++;

        if (
          (cp >= 0x20000 && cp <= 0x2a6df) ||
          (cp >= 0x2a700 && cp <= 0x2b81f) ||
          (cp >= 0x2b820 && cp <= 0x2ebef) ||
          (cp >= 0x2f800 && cp <= 0x2fa1f) ||
          (cp >= 0x30000 && cp <= 0x3134f)
        ) {
          return true;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return false;
}

// --- Winner C: Tiered — best balanced ---
// Two-tier BMP/supplementary dispatch. The c <= 0xFFEF guard separates
// BMP chars from surrogates, so BMP chars never enter the surrogate decode
// path. Slightly more comparisons for CJK Unified (3 vs 2 for MergedFixed)
// but cleaner code flow.
export function isCJKTiered(s) {
  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    const c = s.charCodeAt(i);

    if (c < 0x3000) continue;
    if (c <= 0xffef) {
      if (c <= 0x30ff) return true;                    // Symbols+Hiragana+Katakana
      if (c >= 0x4e00 && c <= 0x9fff) return true;     // CJK Unified
      if (c >= 0x3400 && c <= 0x4dbf) return true;     // Extension A
      if (c >= 0xac00 && c <= 0xd7af) return true;     // Hangul
      if (c >= 0xf900 && c <= 0xfaff) return true;     // Compat Ideographs
      if (c >= 0xff00) return true;                     // Fullwidth (c <= 0xFFEF known)
      continue;
    }

    // Supplementary planes — only reached for surrogates (0xD800+)
    if (c >= 0xd800 && c <= 0xdbff && i + 1 < s.length) {
      const lo = s.charCodeAt(i + 1);

      if (lo >= 0xdc00 && lo <= 0xdfff) {
        const cp = ((c - 0xd800) << 10) + (lo - 0xdc00) + 0x10000;
        i++;

        if (
          (cp >= 0x20000 && cp <= 0x2a6df) ||
          (cp >= 0x2a700 && cp <= 0x2b81f) ||
          (cp >= 0x2b820 && cp <= 0x2ebef) ||
          (cp >= 0x2f800 && cp <= 0x2fa1f) ||
          (cp >= 0x30000 && cp <= 0x3134f)
        ) {
          return true;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return false;
}
```

Presumably `isCJK` is usually false? e.g. you could have an early scan

```
let m = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    m |= s.charCodeAt(i);
}
if (m < 0x3000) return false;
// ... rest of your code ...
```

then most non-CJK scripts would pass quickly.

But also the existing uses of `isCJK` seem quite suboptimal. e.g. at line 763 of `analysis.ts`. it's checking isCJK on every array element twice

Maybe you can try [grapheme-splitter](https://github.com/orling/grapheme-splitter) in non-browser environment.
https://infinitecanvas.cc/guide/lesson-015#cluster

For example in CI Node.js environment:
https://github.com/xiaoiver/infinite-canvas-tutorial/blob/master/__tests__/utils.ts#L149-L152

```ts
import GraphemeSplitter from 'grapheme-splitter';

const splitter = new GraphemeSplitter();
return splitter.splitGraphemes(s);
```

